 The company was formerly known as Everest Re Group, Ltd. and changed its name to Everest Group, Ltd. in July 2023.Everest Group, Ltd., was founded in 1973 and is headquartered in Hamilton, Bermuda.","ceo_bio":"Mr. James Allan Williamson | CEO, President & Director | Age 50 | Compensation: $3.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $5.7M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 9%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $20K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Everest Group, Ltd. is a large-cap financial services business with a $15.8B market cap on $17.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 7% cost of capital, a 4-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 14\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 7.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 17% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7894293535481154},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $3.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"News sentiment running negative (-0.14) across recent coverage","sev":"amber","cat":"news"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 19% margin of safety against estimated fair value","30 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Robbins LLP Urges Everest Group, Ltd. Shareholders Who Lost Money Investing in EG to Contact the Firm About Leading the Class Action","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/robbins-llp-urges-everest-group-ltd-shareholders-who-lost-money-investing-in-eg-to-contact-the-firm-about-leading-the-class-action-302938567.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794545760.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.318,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"INV